  "body": "Replaces #314 by @austin62jake (their commits kept as authored) with main merged in - the fork refuses maintainer pushes.\n\nResolution: `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs` (earlier merge: keep both sides - main's #444 stdio tests and #314's `write_bored_disc_stl` + `detect_holes_fills_a_drill_from_its_model_and_undo_empties_it`); today's merge of `origin/main` had no conflicts (`crates/ui/src/state.rs` auto-merged). `git diff origin/main --stat` shows only #314's own six files.\n\nTargeted gate: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp` 9/9 pass (incl. `detect_holes_fills_a_drill_from_its_model_and_undo_empties_it`, `handshake_and_tool_list`); `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib detect_holes` (CWD crates/ui) 1/1 pass (`detect_holes_refuses_recognizes_and_undo_empties_again`); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Not run: the windowed app, Linux, macOS.\n\nChangelog: The MCP server's new detect_holes tool fills a Drill, Bore or Thread operation's holes from its model, the same way the app's Detect holes button does (#312)\n\nFixes #312\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
